1
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:39,599
The One...The Only...The FABULOUS...

2
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:13,199
Dumbo is a animation, family film directed by Ben Sharpsteen.

3
00:07:40,799 --> 00:07:46,799
Dumbo is a baby elephant born with over-sized ears
and a supreme lack of confidence.

4
00:10:14,399 --> 00:10:20,399
But thanks to his even more diminutive buddy Timothy the Mouse,  the
pint-sized pachyderm learns to surmount all obstacles.

5
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Timothy Q. Mouse (voice) (uncredited), played by Edward Brophy.

6
00:15:21,599 --> 00:15:27,599
Casey Jr. (voice) (uncredited), played by Margaret Wright.

7
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:01,200
Elephant Matriarch / Mrs. Jumbo (voice) (uncredited), played by Verna Felton.

8
00:20:28,799 --> 00:20:34,799
Prissy the Elephant (voice) (uncredited), played by Sarah Selby.

9
00:23:02,399 --> 00:23:08,399
Catty the Elephant (voice) (uncredited), played by Noreen Gammill.

10
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Giddy the Elephant (voice) (uncredited), played by Dorothy Scott.

11
00:28:09,599 --> 00:28:15,599
Dumbo is a 1941 American animated musical fantasy comedy-drama film produced
by Walt Disney Productions and released by RKO Radio Pictures.

12
00:30:43,199 --> 00:30:49,199
The film is based upon the storyline written by Helen Aberson and Harold Pearl, and
illustrated by Helen Durney for the prototype of a novelty toy ("Roll-a-Book").

13
00:33:16,799 --> 00:33:22,799
The main character is Jumbo Jr., an elephant who is ridiculed for his oversized ears and mockingly
nicknamed "Dumbo", but in fact he is capable of flying by using his ears as wings.

14
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:56,400
Throughout most of the film, his only true friend, aside from his mother, is a mouse named Timothy
– a relationship parodying the stereotypical animosity between mice and elephants.

15
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Produced to recoup the financial losses of both Pinocchio and Fantasia,
Dumbo was a deliberate pursuit of simplicity and economy.

16
00:40:57,599 --> 00:41:03,599
At 64 minutes, it is one of the studio's shortest animated features.

17
00:43:31,199 --> 00:43:37,199
Sound was recorded conventionally using the RCA System.

18
00:46:04,799 --> 00:46:10,799
One voice was synthesized using the Sonovox system, but it
too was recorded using the RCA System .

19
00:48:38,400 --> 00:48:44,400
Dumbo was released on October 23, 1941, where it was met with
critical acclaim for its story, humor, visuals, and music.

20
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:18,000
The film was later criticized for stereotyping of black people.

21
00:53:45,599 --> 00:53:51,599
Its accolades include an Academy Award for Best Scoring of a Musical Picture.

22
00:56:19,199 --> 00:56:25,199
In 2017, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically and aesthetically significant".

23
00:58:52,799 --> 00:58:58,799
In the years following its initial release, Dumbo has remained popular, spawning a popular theme park
attraction, merchandise products, a television series, and a live-action adaptation.

24
01:01:26,399 --> 01:01:32,399
The film explores themes of mother, dreams, nightmare, suffering, circus.
